{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c352","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1a0c6-e14d-79a1-9f3c-a04949fbc875"},"sequence":3,"recorded_at":1780531400000002,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","payload_type":"run.model.configured","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_model_configured","command_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3"},"provider_id":"meta","profile_id":"tbh","model_id":"muse-wonder-1.0","display_label":"muse-wonder-1.0","source":"startup"}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c354","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1a0c6-e14d-79a1-9f3c-a04949fbc875"},"sequence":4,"recorded_at":1780531400000004,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3"},"prompt":"Review the updated canonical AX Code Wasm diff API for Desktop integration. READ-ONLY advisory review, no tools needed. Reply in English in under 800 words. The user correctly pointed out this implementation; fresh read at AX Code commit 912c8f92c4d66d0ad8a2887251c3325bbf8b5718 supersedes our earlier duplicate-only assessment. Desktop currently uses Pierre hunk metadata consistently for rendering, navigation, revert and Git staging. We have separately completed a tested Markdown CRLF fix/block-only lex optimization, not a Wasm migration. Do not invent benchmark results. Proposed revised plan: prefer reusing this canonical diff engine, not building another kernel. First owner-supplied independently installable pinned artifact/public API (currently private workspace and depends on workspace util); then read-only worker preview integration with one shared computed snapshot for display/hunk identity, bounded requests, cancellation, stale owner/revision discard; retain existing actions until proven same hunk semantics, then migrate strict hunk reconstruction with file snapshot checks. No sibling source/ignored dist imports or duplicate runtime are permitted. No publication authorized. Identify concrete feasibility issues in API-to-UI mapping, subset/reverse apply correctness, publication packaging, and measurements required before replacing Pierre. Is a dependency-ready prototype possible within current repository rules, or does integration require canonical package delivery first? Source follows.\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/package.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@ax-code/diff-wasm\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Worker-hosted Wasm diff, structured hunks and duplicate comparison using shared Rust kernels\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/browser.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/browser.js\"\n    },\n    \"./node\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/node.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/node.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist\",\n    \"wasm\",\n    \"NOTICE\"\n  ],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"node script/build.mjs\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:browser\": \"node script/browser-smoke.mjs\",\n    \"benchmark\": \"node --import tsx script/benchmark.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@ax-code/util\": \"workspace:*\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@ax-code/diff\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@ax-code/ax-code-reason\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@typescript/native\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"tsx\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"esbuild\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"playwright-core\": \"1.64.1\"\n  }\n}\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/README.md\n# AX Code diff Wasm\n\nAn explicit Node/browser worker API for diff previews, structured hunk\napplication, patch chunks and duplicate comparison. Native AX Code and Wasm\nshare the bounded Rust preview, patch and duplicate kernels. The production\nCLI retains its native backend. This private workspace package is an opt-in\nintegration surface; it is not published to a registry or bundled in CLI\ninstallers.\n\n## Build and validate\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\nrustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown --toolchain stable\ncargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.129 --locked\npnpm install\npnpm build:native diff\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm build\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm typecheck\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm test\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm test:browser\n```\n\nThe build requires the CLI version matching the Rust binding dependency and\nuses rustup's compiler and target libraries even when Homebrew Rust precedes\nit on PATH. `AX_WASM_BINDGEN` may point to the CLI; `AX_DIFF_WASM_TOOLCHAIN`\nselects a rustup toolchain with the Wasm target installed. Generated `dist/`\nand `wasm/` artifacts are ignored; deploy both directories with `NOTICE`.\nTests require real artifacts and the rebuilt native addon. Browser tests use\nPlaywright Chromium or `AX_DIFF_WASM_CHROMIUM` (on macOS, installed Google\nChrome is also detected). Set `AX_DIFF_WASM_BROWSER=firefox` or `webkit`\nto select another engine. Install them with `pnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm\nexec playwright-core install firefox webkit`. CI tests all three browser engines.\n\n## Usage\n\n```ts\nimport { createDiffEngine } from \"@ax-code/diff-wasm/node\"\n// Browser ESM: import from @ax-code/diff-wasm, deploying dist/ and wasm/ together.\n\nconst engine = createDiffEngine()\ntry {\n  const before = \"hello\\r\\n\"\n  const after = \"你好😀\"\n  const preview = await engine.diff(before, after)\n  // { version: 1, additions, deletions, hunks }\n  const result = await engine.applyHunks(before, preview.hunks)\n  // result === after, including the absent final newline.\n  const groups = await engine.compare([[\"a\"], [\"a\", \"b\"], [\"b\"]], 0.5)\n  // Greedy representative groups, not transitive connected components.\n} finally {\n  await engine.close()\n}\n```\n\n`diff` returns one-based structured hunk coordinates, including empty ranges,\nwith four context lines. `applyHunks` requires those exact coordinates, counts\nand source context. It preserves CRLF, Unicode and missing final newlines;\nstale, overlapping or malformed hunks reject atomically. It does not parse\nunified diff files or search fuzzily. Applying a selected subset requires\nrebasing its `newStart` coordinates. `diff(..., { normalize: true })` produces\nLF-normalized hunks while preserving the native API's raw addition/deletion\ncounts; apply those hunks to an explicitly LF-normalized source.\n\n`applyPatch(file, original, chunks)` is a separate API matching the existing\nnative patch worker, including whitespace matching, smart punctuation\nnormalization and final-LF behavior. Chunks contain `old_lines`, `new_lines`,\noptional `change_context` and `is_end_of_file`. It returns computed text only.\nNeither API reads or writes project files. The host retains file snapshots,\npermissions, stale-file checks and all Git/staging operations.\n\nAll methods accept `{ signal, timeoutMs }`. Each engine admits one in-flight\ncall and rejects concurrent calls without queueing. It lazily reuses a worker.\nAbort/deadline terminates that worker; later calls recreate it after successful\ntermination. Request IDs and worker identity exclude stale responses. A failed\nor stuck termination blocks reuse; caller rejection is bounded by a one-second\nteardown grace and retains the original reason. `close()` reports termination\nfailure and may be retried. Always close idle engines. The default operation\ndeadline is 30 seconds (1–120,000 ms), including synchronous bounded admission;\nadmission cannot be interrupted mid-encoding. There is no native or JS fallback\ninside this API. `createDuplicateComparator` is an alias for `createDiffEngine`.\n\nEach text or serialized payload is limited to 16 MiB. Rust also caps combined\ninput, output, lines and algorithmic work. Hunk application accepts at most\n4,096 hunks and 200,000 source/output lines. Duplicate inputs allow 10,000 rows,\n200,000 tokens and 16 MiB JSON, with output capped at 1 MiB. Strings must be\nwell-formed Unicode and thresholds finite. Inputs outside these bounds reject;\nno partial output is returned.\n\nWasm executes synchronously inside a dedicated worker. Cancellation terminates\nthat worker rather than sending it an unread cancellation message. The kernel\nrequires no shared memory, WASI, filesystem, network or process imports. The\nhost loads its own assets. Browser hosting requires module workers, Wasm\ncompilation permission in CSP and the `application/wasm` MIME type. COOP/COEP\nis unnecessary. AX Wiki export CSP is unchanged. The adapted jsdiff code's\nBSD-3-Clause notice is included in `NOTICE`.\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/src/browser.ts\nimport { createClient } from \"./client.js\"\nexport type { CompareOptions, DuplicateComparator, DiffEngine } from \"./client.js\"\nexport type { DuplicateGroup, DiffPreview, Hunk, PatchChunk } from \"./protocol.js\"\n\nexport function createDiffEngine() {\n  return createClient((onMessage, onFailure) => {\n    const worker = new Worker(new URL(\"./browser-worker.js\", import.meta.url), { type: \"module\" })\n    worker.onmessage = (event) => onMessage(event.data)\n    worker.onerror = () => onFailure(new Error(\"Wasm worker failed to load or execute\"))\n    worker.onmessageerror = () => onFailure(new Error(\"Wasm worker message could not be decoded\"))\n    return {\n      post: (message) => worker.postMessage(message),\n      terminate: async () => {\n        worker.terminate()\n      },\n    }\n  })\n}\n\nexport const createDuplicateComparator = createDiffEngine\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/diffHunkRevert.ts\nimport { diffAcceptRejectHunk, parseDiffFromFile, type FileContents, type Hunk } from \"@pierre/diffs\"\n\nfunction toFileContents(fileName: string, contents: string): FileContents {\n  return { name: fileName, contents }\n}\n\nconst EMPTY_HUNKS: Hunk[] = []\nconst HUNK_CACHE_LIMIT = 64\nconst hunkCache = new Map<string, Hunk[]>()\n\n/** 53-bit hash over UTF-16 code units. The cache key never keeps the file text. */\nfunction fileContentHash(input: string): string {\n  let first = 0xdeadbeef\n  let second = 0x41c6ce57\n  for (let index = 0; index < input.length; index += 1) {\n    const unit = input.charCodeAt(index)\n    first = Math.imul(first ^ unit, 2654435761)\n    second = Math.imul(second ^ unit, 1597334677)\n  }\n  first = Math.imul(first ^ (first >>> 16), 2246822507) ^ Math.imul(second ^ (second >>> 13), 3266489909)\n  second = Math.imul(second ^ (second >>> 16), 2246822507) ^ Math.imul(first ^ (first >>> 13), 3266489909)\n  return (4294967296 * (second & 0x1fffff) + (first >>> 0)).toString(16)\n}\n\nfunction fileHunkCacheKey(fileName: string, original: string, modified: string): string {\n  return `${fileName}\\0${original.length}:${fileContentHash(original)}\\0${modified.length}:${fileContentHash(modified)}`\n}\n\nexport function clearFileHunkCache(): void {\n  hunkCache.clear()\n}\n\n/**\n * Parses `original`/`modified` (full file contents) into per-hunk metadata.\n * One entry per path and content hash, shared by the hunk list and review navigation.\n * Two empty sides are not a diff: binary and too-large placeholders skip the parse.\n */\nexport function getFileHunks(original: string, modified: string, fileName = \"\"): Hunk[] {\n  if (original.length === 0 && modified.length === 0) return EMPTY_HUNKS\n  const key = fileHunkCacheKey(fileName, original, modified)\n  const cached = hunkCache.get(key)\n  if (cached) {\n    hunkCache.delete(key)\n    hunkCache.set(key, cached)\n    return cached\n  }\n  const hunks = parseDiffFromFile(toFileContents(fileName, original), toFileContents(fileName, modified)).hunks\n  hunkCache.set(key, hunks)\n  if (hunkCache.size > HUNK_CACHE_LIMIT) {\n    const oldest = hunkCache.keys().next().value\n    if (oldest !== undefined) hunkCache.delete(oldest)\n  }\n  return hunks\n}\n\n/**\n * Reconstructs the file's full content with a single hunk reverted back to\n * `original`, leaving every other hunk's change untouched. `modified` is\n * assumed to already be on disk (the agent writes changes directly), so this\n * is a revert, not a pre-apply \"reject\" the way Copilot Edits/Zed use the term.\n */\nexport function revertHunk(original: string, modified: string, hunkIndex: number, fileName = \"\"): string {\n  const diff = parseDiffFromFile(toFileContents(fileName, original), toFileContents(fileName, modified))\n  // Each entry in `additionLines` already carries its own trailing \"\\n\" (the\n  // last line doesn't, matching whether the file ends with a newline) — join\n  // with \"\" here, not \"\\n\", or every line gets doubled.\n  const resolved = diffAcceptRejectHunk(diff, hunkIndex, \"reject\")\n  return resolved.additionLines.join(\"\")\n}\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/DiffHunkReviewList.tsx\nimport React from \"react\"\nimport { Tooltip, TooltipContent, TooltipTrigger } from \"@/components/ui/tooltip\"\nimport { Icon } from \"@/components/icon/Icon\"\nimport { useI18n } from \"@/lib/i18n\"\nimport { useReviewHunkFocus } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkRegistry\"\nimport { getFileHunks } from \"./diffHunkRevert\"\nimport type { FileDiffHunk } from \"./gitHunkPatch\"\n\ninterface DiffHunkReviewListProps {\n  original: string\n  modified: string\n  fileName?: string\n  onRevertHunk: (hunkIndex: number) => void\n  revertingHunkIndex: number | null\n  /** Hunks of the file's git diff text, matched to rows by new-side start line; omitted hides the per-hunk stage action. */\n  gitHunks?: FileDiffHunk[] | null\n  onStageHunk?: (gitHunkIndex: number) => void\n  stagingHunkIndex?: number | null\n  /** Staged rows unstage their hunk and have no working-tree revert. */\n  staged?: boolean\n}\n\nexport const DiffHunkReviewList: React.FC<DiffHunkReviewListProps> = React.memo(\n  ({\n    original,\n    modified,\n    fileName,\n    onRevertHunk,\n    revertingHunkIndex,\n    gitHunks,\n    onStageHunk,\n    stagingHunkIndex,\n    staged = false,\n  }) => {\n    const { t } = useI18n()\n    const hunkFocus = useReviewHunkFocus(fileName)\n\n    const hunks = React.useMemo(() => getFileHunks(original, modified, fileName ?? \"\"), [original, modified, fileName])\n\n    // Rows come from the diff library's parse of the file contents; the git diff\n    // text's hunks start at the same new-side line whenever both segment the\n    // changes the same way, so a row is offered the action only for the exact\n    // hunk it displays. A row without a match (binary edge cases, segmentation\n    // disagreement) simply shows no action rather than acting on the wrong hunk.\n    const gitHunkIndexByRow = React.useMemo(() => {\n      if (!onStageHunk || !gitHunks) return null\n      const byRow = new Map<number, number>()\n      hunks.forEach((hunk, index) => {\n        const gitHunkIndex = gitHunks.findIndex((candidate) => candidate.newStart === hunk.additionStart)\n        if (gitHunkIndex >= 0) {\n          byRow.set(index, gitHunkIndex)\n        }\n      })\n      return byRow\n    }, [gitHunks, hunks, onStageHunk])\n\n    if (hunks.length === 0) {\n      return null\n    }\n\n    return (\n      <div className=\"flex flex-col border-b border-border/60 bg-[var(--surface-elevated)]\">\n        {hunks.map((hunk, index) => {\n          const isReverting = revertingHunkIndex === index\n          const header = (hunk.hunkSpecs ?? \"\").trim()\n          const gitHunkIndex = gitHunkIndexByRow?.get(index)\n          const hasStageAction = gitHunkIndexByRow != null && gitHunkIndex !== undefined\n          const isStaging = hasStageAction && stagingHunkIndex === gitHunkIndex\n          const stageBusy = stagingHunkIndex != null\n          const active = hunkFocus?.hunkIndex === index\n          return (\n            <div\n              key={`${header}-${index}`}\n              data-review-hunk-index={index}\n              data-review-hunk-focus={active ? \"header\" : undefined}\n              aria-current={active ? \"true\" : undefined}\n              className={`flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border-b border-border/40 last:border-b-0${active ? \" ring-2 ring-inset ring-primary bg-primary/10\" : \"\"}`}\n            >\n              <span className=\"flex-1 min-w-0 truncate font-mono typography-micro text-muted-foreground\">{header}</span>\n              <span className=\"shrink-0 typography-micro\">\n                <span style={{ color: \"var(--status-success)\" }}>+{hunk.additionLines}</span>\n                <span className=\"text-muted-foreground mx-0.5\">/</span>\n                <span style={{ color: \"var(--status-error)\" }}>-{hunk.deletionLines}</span>\n              </span>\n              {hasStageAction && onStageHunk ? (\n                <Tooltip>\n                  <TooltipTrigger asChild>\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      onClick={() => onStageHunk(gitHunkIndex as number)}\n                      disabled={stageBusy}\n                      className=\"flex size-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\"\n                      aria-label={\n                        staged\n                          ? t(\"diffView.hunk.unstageAria\", { hunk: header })\n                          : t(\"diffView.hunk.stageAria\", { hunk: header })\n                      }\n                    >\n                      {isStaging ? (\n                        <Icon name=\"loader-4\" className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n                      ) : (\n                        <Icon name={staged ? \"arrow-down\" : \"arrow-up\"} className=\"size-3.5\" />\n                      )}\n                    </button>\n                  </TooltipTrigger>\n                  <TooltipContent sideOffset={8}>\n                    {staged ? t(\"diffView.hunk.unstageTooltip\") : t(\"diffView.hunk.stageTooltip\")}\n                  </TooltipContent>\n                </Tooltip>\n              ) : null}\n              {staged ? null : (\n                <Tooltip>\n                  <TooltipTrigger asChild>\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      onClick={() => onRevertHunk(index)}\n                      disabled={revertingHunkIndex !== null}\n                      className=\"flex size-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\"\n                      aria-label={t(\"diffView.hunk.revertAria\", { hunk: header })}\n                    >\n                      {isReverting ? (\n                        <Icon name=\"loader-4\" className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n                      ) : (\n                        <Icon name=\"arrow-go-back\" className=\"size-3.5\" />\n                      )}\n                    </button>\n                  </TooltipTrigger>\n                  <TooltipContent sideOffset={8}>{t(\"diffView.hunk.revertTooltip\")}</TooltipContent>\n                </Tooltip>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )\n        })}\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n)\n\nDiffHunkReviewList.displayName = \"DiffHunkReviewList\"\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/usePublishReviewHunks.ts\nimport { useEffect } from \"react\"\n\nimport { publishReviewHunks, releaseReviewHunks, retainReviewHunks, useReviewHunkScope } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkRegistry\"\nimport { reviewHunkAnchors } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkNavigation\"\n\nimport { getFileHunks } from \"./diffHunkRevert\"\n\n/**\n * Measure one file's hunk list from the same parse Pierre uses to draw it.\n * Pass null contents for a binary, image, or too-large file: those have no hunks and are not parsed.\n */\nexport function ReviewHunkMeasure(props: { path: string; original: string | null; modified: string | null }) {\n  usePublishReviewHunks(props.path, props.original, props.modified)\n  return null\n}\n\n/** Measure one file's rendered hunk list from the same parse Pierre uses to draw it. */\nexport function usePublishReviewHunks(\n  path: string | null | undefined,\n  original: string | null,\n  modified: string | null,\n): void {\n  const scope = useReviewHunkScope()\n  const scopeId = scope?.id\n  const directory = scope?.directory ?? \"\"\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!path || !scopeId) return\n    retainReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path)\n    const anchors =\n      original === null || modified === null ? [] : reviewHunkAnchors(getFileHunks(original, modified, path))\n    publishReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path, anchors)\n    return () => releaseReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path)\n  }, [directory, modified, original, path, scopeId])\n}\n"}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c356","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1a0c6-e14d-79a1-9f3c-a04949fbc875"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000006,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","payload_type":"run.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_started","command_id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a1a0c6-e5b9-72d2-a84b-96a08eea60a3"},"prompt":"Review the updated canonical AX Code Wasm diff API for Desktop integration. READ-ONLY advisory review, no tools needed. Reply in English in under 800 words. The user correctly pointed out this implementation; fresh read at AX Code commit 912c8f92c4d66d0ad8a2887251c3325bbf8b5718 supersedes our earlier duplicate-only assessment. Desktop currently uses Pierre hunk metadata consistently for rendering, navigation, revert and Git staging. We have separately completed a tested Markdown CRLF fix/block-only lex optimization, not a Wasm migration. Do not invent benchmark results. Proposed revised plan: prefer reusing this canonical diff engine, not building another kernel. First owner-supplied independently installable pinned artifact/public API (currently private workspace and depends on workspace util); then read-only worker preview integration with one shared computed snapshot for display/hunk identity, bounded requests, cancellation, stale owner/revision discard; retain existing actions until proven same hunk semantics, then migrate strict hunk reconstruction with file snapshot checks. No sibling source/ignored dist imports or duplicate runtime are permitted. No publication authorized. Identify concrete feasibility issues in API-to-UI mapping, subset/reverse apply correctness, publication packaging, and measurements required before replacing Pierre. Is a dependency-ready prototype possible within current repository rules, or does integration require canonical package delivery first? Source follows.\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/package.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@ax-code/diff-wasm\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Worker-hosted Wasm diff, structured hunks and duplicate comparison using shared Rust kernels\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/browser.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/browser.js\"\n    },\n    \"./node\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/node.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/node.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist\",\n    \"wasm\",\n    \"NOTICE\"\n  ],\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"node script/build.mjs\",\n    \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n    \"test:browser\": \"node script/browser-smoke.mjs\",\n    \"benchmark\": \"node --import tsx script/benchmark.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@ax-code/util\": \"workspace:*\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@ax-code/diff\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@ax-code/ax-code-reason\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@typescript/native\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"tsx\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"esbuild\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"playwright-core\": \"1.64.1\"\n  }\n}\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/README.md\n# AX Code diff Wasm\n\nAn explicit Node/browser worker API for diff previews, structured hunk\napplication, patch chunks and duplicate comparison. Native AX Code and Wasm\nshare the bounded Rust preview, patch and duplicate kernels. The production\nCLI retains its native backend. This private workspace package is an opt-in\nintegration surface; it is not published to a registry or bundled in CLI\ninstallers.\n\n## Build and validate\n\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\nrustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown --toolchain stable\ncargo install wasm-bindgen-cli --version 0.2.129 --locked\npnpm install\npnpm build:native diff\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm build\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm typecheck\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm test\npnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm test:browser\n```\n\nThe build requires the CLI version matching the Rust binding dependency and\nuses rustup's compiler and target libraries even when Homebrew Rust precedes\nit on PATH. `AX_WASM_BINDGEN` may point to the CLI; `AX_DIFF_WASM_TOOLCHAIN`\nselects a rustup toolchain with the Wasm target installed. Generated `dist/`\nand `wasm/` artifacts are ignored; deploy both directories with `NOTICE`.\nTests require real artifacts and the rebuilt native addon. Browser tests use\nPlaywright Chromium or `AX_DIFF_WASM_CHROMIUM` (on macOS, installed Google\nChrome is also detected). Set `AX_DIFF_WASM_BROWSER=firefox` or `webkit`\nto select another engine. Install them with `pnpm --dir packages/ax-code-diff-wasm\nexec playwright-core install firefox webkit`. CI tests all three browser engines.\n\n## Usage\n\n```ts\nimport { createDiffEngine } from \"@ax-code/diff-wasm/node\"\n// Browser ESM: import from @ax-code/diff-wasm, deploying dist/ and wasm/ together.\n\nconst engine = createDiffEngine()\ntry {\n  const before = \"hello\\r\\n\"\n  const after = \"你好😀\"\n  const preview = await engine.diff(before, after)\n  // { version: 1, additions, deletions, hunks }\n  const result = await engine.applyHunks(before, preview.hunks)\n  // result === after, including the absent final newline.\n  const groups = await engine.compare([[\"a\"], [\"a\", \"b\"], [\"b\"]], 0.5)\n  // Greedy representative groups, not transitive connected components.\n} finally {\n  await engine.close()\n}\n```\n\n`diff` returns one-based structured hunk coordinates, including empty ranges,\nwith four context lines. `applyHunks` requires those exact coordinates, counts\nand source context. It preserves CRLF, Unicode and missing final newlines;\nstale, overlapping or malformed hunks reject atomically. It does not parse\nunified diff files or search fuzzily. Applying a selected subset requires\nrebasing its `newStart` coordinates. `diff(..., { normalize: true })` produces\nLF-normalized hunks while preserving the native API's raw addition/deletion\ncounts; apply those hunks to an explicitly LF-normalized source.\n\n`applyPatch(file, original, chunks)` is a separate API matching the existing\nnative patch worker, including whitespace matching, smart punctuation\nnormalization and final-LF behavior. Chunks contain `old_lines`, `new_lines`,\noptional `change_context` and `is_end_of_file`. It returns computed text only.\nNeither API reads or writes project files. The host retains file snapshots,\npermissions, stale-file checks and all Git/staging operations.\n\nAll methods accept `{ signal, timeoutMs }`. Each engine admits one in-flight\ncall and rejects concurrent calls without queueing. It lazily reuses a worker.\nAbort/deadline terminates that worker; later calls recreate it after successful\ntermination. Request IDs and worker identity exclude stale responses. A failed\nor stuck termination blocks reuse; caller rejection is bounded by a one-second\nteardown grace and retains the original reason. `close()` reports termination\nfailure and may be retried. Always close idle engines. The default operation\ndeadline is 30 seconds (1–120,000 ms), including synchronous bounded admission;\nadmission cannot be interrupted mid-encoding. There is no native or JS fallback\ninside this API. `createDuplicateComparator` is an alias for `createDiffEngine`.\n\nEach text or serialized payload is limited to 16 MiB. Rust also caps combined\ninput, output, lines and algorithmic work. Hunk application accepts at most\n4,096 hunks and 200,000 source/output lines. Duplicate inputs allow 10,000 rows,\n200,000 tokens and 16 MiB JSON, with output capped at 1 MiB. Strings must be\nwell-formed Unicode and thresholds finite. Inputs outside these bounds reject;\nno partial output is returned.\n\nWasm executes synchronously inside a dedicated worker. Cancellation terminates\nthat worker rather than sending it an unread cancellation message. The kernel\nrequires no shared memory, WASI, filesystem, network or process imports. The\nhost loads its own assets. Browser hosting requires module workers, Wasm\ncompilation permission in CSP and the `application/wasm` MIME type. COOP/COEP\nis unnecessary. AX Wiki export CSP is unchanged. The adapted jsdiff code's\nBSD-3-Clause notice is included in `NOTICE`.\n\nFILE packages/ax-code-diff-wasm/src/browser.ts\nimport { createClient } from \"./client.js\"\nexport type { CompareOptions, DuplicateComparator, DiffEngine } from \"./client.js\"\nexport type { DuplicateGroup, DiffPreview, Hunk, PatchChunk } from \"./protocol.js\"\n\nexport function createDiffEngine() {\n  return createClient((onMessage, onFailure) => {\n    const worker = new Worker(new URL(\"./browser-worker.js\", import.meta.url), { type: \"module\" })\n    worker.onmessage = (event) => onMessage(event.data)\n    worker.onerror = () => onFailure(new Error(\"Wasm worker failed to load or execute\"))\n    worker.onmessageerror = () => onFailure(new Error(\"Wasm worker message could not be decoded\"))\n    return {\n      post: (message) => worker.postMessage(message),\n      terminate: async () => {\n        worker.terminate()\n      },\n    }\n  })\n}\n\nexport const createDuplicateComparator = createDiffEngine\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/diffHunkRevert.ts\nimport { diffAcceptRejectHunk, parseDiffFromFile, type FileContents, type Hunk } from \"@pierre/diffs\"\n\nfunction toFileContents(fileName: string, contents: string): FileContents {\n  return { name: fileName, contents }\n}\n\nconst EMPTY_HUNKS: Hunk[] = []\nconst HUNK_CACHE_LIMIT = 64\nconst hunkCache = new Map<string, Hunk[]>()\n\n/** 53-bit hash over UTF-16 code units. The cache key never keeps the file text. */\nfunction fileContentHash(input: string): string {\n  let first = 0xdeadbeef\n  let second = 0x41c6ce57\n  for (let index = 0; index < input.length; index += 1) {\n    const unit = input.charCodeAt(index)\n    first = Math.imul(first ^ unit, 2654435761)\n    second = Math.imul(second ^ unit, 1597334677)\n  }\n  first = Math.imul(first ^ (first >>> 16), 2246822507) ^ Math.imul(second ^ (second >>> 13), 3266489909)\n  second = Math.imul(second ^ (second >>> 16), 2246822507) ^ Math.imul(first ^ (first >>> 13), 3266489909)\n  return (4294967296 * (second & 0x1fffff) + (first >>> 0)).toString(16)\n}\n\nfunction fileHunkCacheKey(fileName: string, original: string, modified: string): string {\n  return `${fileName}\\0${original.length}:${fileContentHash(original)}\\0${modified.length}:${fileContentHash(modified)}`\n}\n\nexport function clearFileHunkCache(): void {\n  hunkCache.clear()\n}\n\n/**\n * Parses `original`/`modified` (full file contents) into per-hunk metadata.\n * One entry per path and content hash, shared by the hunk list and review navigation.\n * Two empty sides are not a diff: binary and too-large placeholders skip the parse.\n */\nexport function getFileHunks(original: string, modified: string, fileName = \"\"): Hunk[] {\n  if (original.length === 0 && modified.length === 0) return EMPTY_HUNKS\n  const key = fileHunkCacheKey(fileName, original, modified)\n  const cached = hunkCache.get(key)\n  if (cached) {\n    hunkCache.delete(key)\n    hunkCache.set(key, cached)\n    return cached\n  }\n  const hunks = parseDiffFromFile(toFileContents(fileName, original), toFileContents(fileName, modified)).hunks\n  hunkCache.set(key, hunks)\n  if (hunkCache.size > HUNK_CACHE_LIMIT) {\n    const oldest = hunkCache.keys().next().value\n    if (oldest !== undefined) hunkCache.delete(oldest)\n  }\n  return hunks\n}\n\n/**\n * Reconstructs the file's full content with a single hunk reverted back to\n * `original`, leaving every other hunk's change untouched. `modified` is\n * assumed to already be on disk (the agent writes changes directly), so this\n * is a revert, not a pre-apply \"reject\" the way Copilot Edits/Zed use the term.\n */\nexport function revertHunk(original: string, modified: string, hunkIndex: number, fileName = \"\"): string {\n  const diff = parseDiffFromFile(toFileContents(fileName, original), toFileContents(fileName, modified))\n  // Each entry in `additionLines` already carries its own trailing \"\\n\" (the\n  // last line doesn't, matching whether the file ends with a newline) — join\n  // with \"\" here, not \"\\n\", or every line gets doubled.\n  const resolved = diffAcceptRejectHunk(diff, hunkIndex, \"reject\")\n  return resolved.additionLines.join(\"\")\n}\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/DiffHunkReviewList.tsx\nimport React from \"react\"\nimport { Tooltip, TooltipContent, TooltipTrigger } from \"@/components/ui/tooltip\"\nimport { Icon } from \"@/components/icon/Icon\"\nimport { useI18n } from \"@/lib/i18n\"\nimport { useReviewHunkFocus } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkRegistry\"\nimport { getFileHunks } from \"./diffHunkRevert\"\nimport type { FileDiffHunk } from \"./gitHunkPatch\"\n\ninterface DiffHunkReviewListProps {\n  original: string\n  modified: string\n  fileName?: string\n  onRevertHunk: (hunkIndex: number) => void\n  revertingHunkIndex: number | null\n  /** Hunks of the file's git diff text, matched to rows by new-side start line; omitted hides the per-hunk stage action. */\n  gitHunks?: FileDiffHunk[] | null\n  onStageHunk?: (gitHunkIndex: number) => void\n  stagingHunkIndex?: number | null\n  /** Staged rows unstage their hunk and have no working-tree revert. */\n  staged?: boolean\n}\n\nexport const DiffHunkReviewList: React.FC<DiffHunkReviewListProps> = React.memo(\n  ({\n    original,\n    modified,\n    fileName,\n    onRevertHunk,\n    revertingHunkIndex,\n    gitHunks,\n    onStageHunk,\n    stagingHunkIndex,\n    staged = false,\n  }) => {\n    const { t } = useI18n()\n    const hunkFocus = useReviewHunkFocus(fileName)\n\n    const hunks = React.useMemo(() => getFileHunks(original, modified, fileName ?? \"\"), [original, modified, fileName])\n\n    // Rows come from the diff library's parse of the file contents; the git diff\n    // text's hunks start at the same new-side line whenever both segment the\n    // changes the same way, so a row is offered the action only for the exact\n    // hunk it displays. A row without a match (binary edge cases, segmentation\n    // disagreement) simply shows no action rather than acting on the wrong hunk.\n    const gitHunkIndexByRow = React.useMemo(() => {\n      if (!onStageHunk || !gitHunks) return null\n      const byRow = new Map<number, number>()\n      hunks.forEach((hunk, index) => {\n        const gitHunkIndex = gitHunks.findIndex((candidate) => candidate.newStart === hunk.additionStart)\n        if (gitHunkIndex >= 0) {\n          byRow.set(index, gitHunkIndex)\n        }\n      })\n      return byRow\n    }, [gitHunks, hunks, onStageHunk])\n\n    if (hunks.length === 0) {\n      return null\n    }\n\n    return (\n      <div className=\"flex flex-col border-b border-border/60 bg-[var(--surface-elevated)]\">\n        {hunks.map((hunk, index) => {\n          const isReverting = revertingHunkIndex === index\n          const header = (hunk.hunkSpecs ?? \"\").trim()\n          const gitHunkIndex = gitHunkIndexByRow?.get(index)\n          const hasStageAction = gitHunkIndexByRow != null && gitHunkIndex !== undefined\n          const isStaging = hasStageAction && stagingHunkIndex === gitHunkIndex\n          const stageBusy = stagingHunkIndex != null\n          const active = hunkFocus?.hunkIndex === index\n          return (\n            <div\n              key={`${header}-${index}`}\n              data-review-hunk-index={index}\n              data-review-hunk-focus={active ? \"header\" : undefined}\n              aria-current={active ? \"true\" : undefined}\n              className={`flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border-b border-border/40 last:border-b-0${active ? \" ring-2 ring-inset ring-primary bg-primary/10\" : \"\"}`}\n            >\n              <span className=\"flex-1 min-w-0 truncate font-mono typography-micro text-muted-foreground\">{header}</span>\n              <span className=\"shrink-0 typography-micro\">\n                <span style={{ color: \"var(--status-success)\" }}>+{hunk.additionLines}</span>\n                <span className=\"text-muted-foreground mx-0.5\">/</span>\n                <span style={{ color: \"var(--status-error)\" }}>-{hunk.deletionLines}</span>\n              </span>\n              {hasStageAction && onStageHunk ? (\n                <Tooltip>\n                  <TooltipTrigger asChild>\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      onClick={() => onStageHunk(gitHunkIndex as number)}\n                      disabled={stageBusy}\n                      className=\"flex size-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\"\n                      aria-label={\n                        staged\n                          ? t(\"diffView.hunk.unstageAria\", { hunk: header })\n                          : t(\"diffView.hunk.stageAria\", { hunk: header })\n                      }\n                    >\n                      {isStaging ? (\n                        <Icon name=\"loader-4\" className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n                      ) : (\n                        <Icon name={staged ? \"arrow-down\" : \"arrow-up\"} className=\"size-3.5\" />\n                      )}\n                    </button>\n                  </TooltipTrigger>\n                  <TooltipContent sideOffset={8}>\n                    {staged ? t(\"diffView.hunk.unstageTooltip\") : t(\"diffView.hunk.stageTooltip\")}\n                  </TooltipContent>\n                </Tooltip>\n              ) : null}\n              {staged ? null : (\n                <Tooltip>\n                  <TooltipTrigger asChild>\n                    <button\n                      type=\"button\"\n                      onClick={() => onRevertHunk(index)}\n                      disabled={revertingHunkIndex !== null}\n                      className=\"flex size-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\"\n                      aria-label={t(\"diffView.hunk.revertAria\", { hunk: header })}\n                    >\n                      {isReverting ? (\n                        <Icon name=\"loader-4\" className=\"size-3.5 animate-spin\" />\n                      ) : (\n                        <Icon name=\"arrow-go-back\" className=\"size-3.5\" />\n                      )}\n                    </button>\n                  </TooltipTrigger>\n                  <TooltipContent sideOffset={8}>{t(\"diffView.hunk.revertTooltip\")}</TooltipContent>\n                </Tooltip>\n              )}\n            </div>\n          )\n        })}\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n)\n\nDiffHunkReviewList.displayName = \"DiffHunkReviewList\"\n\nFILE desktop/packages/ui/src/components/views/usePublishReviewHunks.ts\nimport { useEffect } from \"react\"\n\nimport { publishReviewHunks, releaseReviewHunks, retainReviewHunks, useReviewHunkScope } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkRegistry\"\nimport { reviewHunkAnchors } from \"@/lib/reviewHunkNavigation\"\n\nimport { getFileHunks } from \"./diffHunkRevert\"\n\n/**\n * Measure one file's hunk list from the same parse Pierre uses to draw it.\n * Pass null contents for a binary, image, or too-large file: those have no hunks and are not parsed.\n */\nexport function ReviewHunkMeasure(props: { path: string; original: string | null; modified: string | null }) {\n  usePublishReviewHunks(props.path, props.original, props.modified)\n  return null\n}\n\n/** Measure one file's rendered hunk list from the same parse Pierre uses to draw it. */\nexport function usePublishReviewHunks(\n  path: string | null | undefined,\n  original: string | null,\n  modified: string | null,\n): void {\n  const scope = useReviewHunkScope()\n  const scopeId = scope?.id\n  const directory = scope?.directory ?? \"\"\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!path || !scopeId) return\n    retainReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path)\n    const anchors =\n      original === null || modified === null ? [] : reviewHunkAnchors(getFileHunks(original, modified, path))\n    publishReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path, anchors)\n    return () => releaseReviewHunks(scopeId, directory, path)\n  }, [directory, modified, original, path, scopeId])\n}\n"}}
